WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.800
Ninety-four Truth and Reconciliation Calls to Action.

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:08.488
By 2024, approximately thirteen have been fully implemented.

00:00:08.488 --> 00:00:12.965
Two hundred and thirty-one MMIWG Calls for Justice — implementation stalled.

00:00:12.965 --> 00:00:19.897
Twenty-eight long-term drinking water advisories remain active according to Indigenous Services Canada in 2024.

00:00:19.897 --> 00:00:25.181
The department spent eighteen point nine billion dollars in 2022-23.

00:00:25.181 --> 00:00:27.056
The spending goes up.

00:00:27.056 --> 00:00:29.147
The outcomes do not.

00:00:29.147 --> 00:00:35.670
One thousand one hundred and eighty-one RCMP-documented missing or murdered Indigenous women and girls.

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:42.113
The national inquiry cost ninety-two million dollars between 2016 and 2019.

00:00:42.113 --> 00:00:51.238
Indigenous women represent four percent of the female population and twenty-four percent of female homicide victims — a homicide rate four times the national average.

00:00:51.238 --> 00:01:00.556
Highway 16 — the Highway of Tears — stretches seven hundred and twenty-four kilometres with over forty women and girls missing or murdered since 1970.

00:01:00.556 --> 00:01:03.329
Reconciliation is not a slogan.

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:07.579
It is a measurable commitment — and by every measure, Canada is failing.
